 "licenceNotes": "The repository is MIT-licensed and documents these files as anonymized hand history logs scraped from July 1 to 23, 2009 and uploaded by HandHQ. The rights of the original poker sites or players in the underlying logs are not stated by the repository; player names are replaced by hashes. Used here offline, for aggregate statistics only: no hand, player hash or raw file is committed or redistributed, and nothing is sent anywhere.",
 "access": "needs-approval",
 "approvedBy": "user instruction (Phase 2.5 brief: discover, verify and download PHH cash-game datasets)",
 "approvedOn": "2026-11-18",
 "retrieved": "2026-11-19",
 "population": "Online no-limit hold'em cash games, July 1-25 2009: PokerStars 200NL, iPoker Network 100NL and 200NL, Absolute Poker 100NL; 6-max and full-ring tables (heads-up tables excluded); human players.",
 "labelSemantics": "human-action",
 "caveats": [
  "Heads-up tables are excluded: the conversion lists p1 as small blind but p2 acts first before the flop, so blinds or order are wrong.",
  "iPoker files do not record stacks (written inf): replayed with 1,000 big blinds each, flagged stacksUnknown, stack-to-pot ratio missing.",
  "Hole cards are known only when shown at showdown (or written in the deal line for a showdown hand): a selected sample, never used as known otherwise.",
  "Online play from 2009: population behaviour may differ from present-day PokerNow games; rake and site rules are not recorded per hand.",
  "Players are anonymised hashes; nothing about individuals is inferred or kept outside data/."
